description:
A single mutation-session retry contract lives in the command layer: the retry bound, apply-conflict classification, and the terminal conflict error each in one place, ready for command sites to adopt.

## Background

The command layer hand-copies a capture/plan/apply/retry protocol across sixteen command files: `for _ in 0..8` loops, `Err(RetryableConflict{..}) => continue` match arms, and bespoke "did not converge" bail messages. This task builds the shared contract that retires that duplication; migrating the individual call sites is separate work.

Add to `crates/jit/src/commands/mod.rs`:

```rust
const MUTATION_SESSION_RETRY_LIMIT: usize = 8;

#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]
#[error("{operation} did not converge after {attempts} capture conflicts")]
pub struct MutationSessionExhausted { operation: &'static str, attempts: usize }

enum AttemptOutcome<T> { Done(T), Retry }

// The single apply-conflict classifier - the only place a RetryableConflict on
// apply is interpreted.
fn classify_apply<T>(outcome: Result<impl Sized, RepositoryStateStoreError>, value: T)
    -> Result<AttemptOutcome<T>>;

// Retry driver: owns the bound and terminal error, holds NO session, so a
// closure may open/release sessions, take a claims guard, and run a subprocess
// between them.
fn with_mutation_attempts<T>(operation: &'static str,
    attempt: impl FnMut() -> Result<AttemptOutcome<T>>) -> Result<T>;

// Session-passed convenience: opens one fresh recovered session per attempt and
// applies Apply(plan) via classify_apply.
enum SessionStep<T> { Apply(MaterializationPlan, T), Done(T), Retry }

fn with_mutation_session<S: RepositoryStateStore, T>(
    store: &S, layout: &RepositoryLayout, operation: &'static str,
    attempt: impl FnMut(&mut dyn RepositoryMutationSession) -> Result<SessionStep<T>>,
) -> Result<T>;
```

`with_mutation_attempts` owns the single retry bound (one named constant) and the typed terminal `MutationSessionExhausted`. `classify_apply` owns apply-conflict classification. A shared `capture_or_retry` helper folds a capture `RetryableConflict` into a retry signal for sites that classify capture conflicts inline. The entry points are free `fn`s generic over the store because at least one call site is a free function rather than a method. `MutationSessionExhausted` maps to the generic exit code through a single arm contributed to the exit-code mapping in `crates/jit/src/main.rs`.

## Success Criteria

- [hard] REQ-01: `MUTATION_SESSION_RETRY_LIMIT`, `MutationSessionExhausted`, `AttemptOutcome`, `classify_apply`, `with_mutation_attempts`, `SessionStep`, `with_mutation_session`, and `capture_or_retry` exist in the command layer with the signatures above; the retry bound, apply-conflict classification, and terminal conflict error each live in exactly one place.
- [hard] REQ-02: Conflict-classification unit tests exercise `classify_apply` and `with_mutation_attempts` directly.
- [hard] REQ-03: `MutationSessionExhausted` is mapped to its exit code by a single arm in the `crates/jit/src/main.rs` exit-code mapping.
- [hard] REQ-04: The existing failure-injection and interruption tests continue to pass; the contract is behavior-preserving.

## Notes

Migrating the individual retry loops onto these combinators is out of this task's scope. `with_mutation_attempts` deliberately holds no session so a caller can release a preflight session, take a claims guard, and run an external subprocess between attempts without inverting lock ordering.
